    {
      "subject": "logical_mask_vs_visible_mesh",
      "finding": "Gameplay island is five land cells, but its visible shoreline is not a simple union of axis-aligned cells. The inferred northern edge reaches approximately grid y0.70; visible west/east shoulders reach approximately x1.77 and x4.22. The north value is canopy-occluded and must not be scored as ground truth. Projection and mesh displacement also affect this inverse mapping."
    },
    {
      "subject": "northwest_concavity",
      "finding": "The concavity between northern forest cell [1,3] and western tree cells [2,2]/[3,2] is asymmetric. It forms a short west-east shoulder near source y264, then turns north around x638. Crowns hide part of the precise ground bend; its interpolation is marked inferred."
    },
    {
      "subject": "east_profile",
      "finding": "Visible east coast makes a large convex bulge around y260-290, tightens into a waist near x750/y350, then bulges outward again around x761/y390. It is not one repeated rounded-corner shape."
    },
    {
      "subject": "west_profile",
      "finding": "Western coast has two shallow indentations near y315 and y395 with a broader westward shoulder near y355-370. Preserve these low-frequency shifts; tiny edge texture is not reliable enough to digitize exactly."
    },
    {
      "subject": "shallow_water_band",
      "finding": "A pale cyan/gray-green shallow halo sits outside the cream wet-beach edge, generally about 5-18 source pixels where visible. Its outer boundary is feathered rather than a second hard contour. Width/color are approximate because JPEG blur, shadows and cultural tint overlap it."
    },
    {
      "subject": "beach_width",
      "finding": "Cream beach is visibly variable: commonly roughly 5-15 source pixels, locally approaching 15-20 on broad exposed shoulders, and nearly hidden under canopy on the north/northwest. It should not be a constant-width pale stroke. Measurements are visual ranges, not exact per-vertex widths."
    },
    {
      "subject": "beach_inner_edge",
      "finding": "Beach-to-grass transition is broad and irregular, with grass reaching closer to water in several places than at the southwest and eastern shoulders. No inner-beach polygon is asserted where trees or city art hide it."
    },
    {
      "subject": "overlays",
      "finding": "Purple ownership boundary/tint, cyan unit-selection ring, city label and resource bubbles are overlays. None is a water depth band or land boundary. The outer shoreline remains separate from them."
    },
    {
      "subject": "projection",
      "finding": "All source pixels refer to unmodified 1400x788 WCLT-14.jpg. Fractional grid coordinates are an approximate inverse of the perspective grid, not a camera-calibrated orthographic reconstruction."
    },
